    <div class="eyebrow">ABOUT / LESS IS MORE</div>
    <h1>Use AI to remove complexity.<br />Keep only what matters.</h1>
    <p class="dek">Hi, I’m tinylion1024, a minimalist AI product builder.</p>
    <div class="essay-rule"></div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>I care about one question: how can clearer judgment, shorter workflows, and fewer tools turn a product idea into something people actually use?</p>
      <p>Minimalism is not doing less for its own sake. It is continually identifying what does not matter. Product judgment chooses what deserves to exist, AI shortens the path to delivery, and growth tests that judgment against real behavior.</p>
      <p>This site is not a résumé or a feed. It is where I document product decisions, AI building workflows, growth experiments, and the complexity that can be removed.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="principles" aria-label="My working principles">
      <div><span>01 / JUDGE</span><p>Decide what not to build.</p></div>
      <div><span>02 / BUILD</span><p>Use AI to shorten the distance from idea to product.</p></div>
      <div><span>03 / VERIFY</span><p>Test judgment against real use and growth.</p></div>
    </div>
